target:    composer.json
gate:      composer test:composer-script-closure
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    is reachable from neither test:all nor the standalone list
rationale: Drops test:no-orphan-test-files from the test:all closure while leaving its definition. The script then runs only if someone types it -- the state test:fp-negative-linux was found in, reachable from nothing and running nowhere, which the file-level orphan gate cannot see because it only asks whether a FILE is named. Regenerated at context=1 on 2026-09-04: the first version carried four neighbouring aggregate entries as context and stopped applying the moment a new script was inserted anywhere near it.
---
--- a/composer.json
+++ b/composer.json
@@ -372,3 +372,2 @@
       "@test:migration-notice-visibility",
-      "@test:no-orphan-test-files",
       "@test:composer-script-closure",
